const e="yagp-2026",d=2026,a="Built from the YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations (19 sections). The document prints no semi-final venues or dates (the website lists them), no judging mark weights, and no points for placings. Fees and dates are for the 2025-2026 season (Fall 2025 and Winter/Spring 2026 venues) and are Variables. The finance and regional e-mail addresses are the organiser's printed office addresses; no personal contact or bank detail is printed. Dancers aged 9-20 are counted on 1 January 2026. The Classical Repertoire List is kept per age group under Allowed, with the printed restrictions.",n=JSON.parse(`{"Title":"Rules & Criteria","Subtitle":"Youth America Grand Prix 2026: regional semi-finals and the Finals. Read these rules before you register.","NoticeTitle":"Please Read Before Registering","Notice":"Register online at {{Website}}. Ages for the whole season are counted on {{SeasonAgeDate}}. YAGP can deduct points from any entry or dancer that does not follow the rules. Registration fee: {{AdminFee}}.","Notes":["Semi-final venues and dates: {{SemiFinalVenues}}.","Music deadline: {{MusicDeadline}}. Entry updates: {{UpdateDeadline}}.","News: {{Notice}}"],"Sections":[{"Key":"general","Title":"General Rules","Items":["YAGP follows all guidelines from the U.S. government, state and local or city governments and theater policies for the health and safety of participants.","Follow the YAGP website and its social media (Facebook, Instagram, YouTube) for news, live-streaming of events, registration information and updates.","Dancers may enter as soloists, as part of an ensemble, in a pas de deux, or in any mix of these.","Dancers may register at more than one semi-final location, if space is available at each place.","Dancers may perform more than one variation. YAGP can limit the number of variations a student performs, limit the events a student attends, or decline any registration, depending on space.","All solo dancers choose Classical Ballet, Contemporary/Open Dance, or both.","Classical Ballet: the variation must come from the Classical Repertoire List.","Contemporary/Open Dance: any non-classical ballet solo. Music is not limited to instrumental tracks and may have appropriate lyrics.","In the Classical Ballet category at any regional semi-final, dancers must pick their variation from the Classical Repertoire List for their age group.","The dancer is responsible for getting approval to present choreography for any variation that needs approval, as listed at the end of the Classical Repertoire List.","A pas de deux from the Classical Repertoire List may be performed as Adagio and Coda only.","Dancers who place at a semi-final may receive scholarship offers or letters of interest or acceptance. They follow up directly with the contact given by the presenting school.","Master classes with YAGP jury members and master teachers are free, part of the YAGP educational mission, and not required. Not attending does not change a dancer's score or standing.","YAGP can make photo and video recordings at any time during any YAGP event, including master classes, rehearsals, performances, the lobby and backstage. Dancers, parents and legal guardians give permission for this, and for use of the recordings (with name or likeness) in YAGP promotion in print, online and on social media.","If an event must be held virtually for health and safety, dancers are told by e-mail, and the information is posted on the YAGP website and announced on social media.","Props: backstage space is often limited, so use the minimum number of props. Theaters may limit props. Props are used at the dancer's own risk.","YAGP does not provide storage for props, help moving them on or off stage, help shipping them before or after a competition, and is not responsible for lost props.","YAGP and the host venue are not responsible for personal injury or property loss. YAGP can move a competition site, date or time, or make an event multi-day.","YAGP can change, delete or add rules, regulations or policies at any time. It can cancel an event because of low registration, weather or other unforeseen circumstances.","If YAGP cancels an event and does not reschedule it, refunds or credits for the next year are given. If the event is rescheduled, no refunds are given. Check the website and your registration e-mail for updates.","All changes to submitted entries must be made in the registration platform. Verbal or e-mail requests are not accepted.","By signing the YAGP Release Agreement, all competitors let YAGP and its representatives publish their photographs and videos on local or national television, promotional videos, marketing materials, the internet or any other visual media to promote its competitions. Staff and representatives are released from claims for damages or injuries while taking part in or attending any YAGP activity. Photographs and videos taken by YAGP and its representatives belong to YAGP."]},{"Key":"eligibility","Title":"Eligibility","Items":["YAGP 2026 is open to dance students of all nationalities, aged 9-20.","Younger or older students may take part in the Ensemble or Pas de Deux category, as long as the average age of the dancers falls between 9 and 20.","A dancer's age for the whole YAGP 2026 season is counted strictly on {{SeasonAgeDate}}.","Professional dancers may not compete. A professional dancer is anyone employed as a full-time dancer (apprentices included) with a professional dance company on a yearly contract of at least 26 weeks a year. This includes dancers who are not employed under such a contract now but have been in the past.","In an ensemble or pas de deux, a partner may not be a professional dancer (any apprentice, trainee, part-time or full-time dancer with a professional dance company).","Senior age division: 15-20 years old (born between 2 January 2006 and 1 January 2011).","Junior age division: 12-14 years old (born between 2 January 2011 and 1 January 2014).","Pre-Competitive age division: 9-11 years old (born between 2 January 2014 and 1 January 2017).","Ensemble division: the average age of the ensemble must be between 9 and 20.","A dancer may enter as an individual dancer or as a dancer representing a school, or the school representative may register all dancers.","Students aged 10 and under may not perform en pointe. If they do, they are not eligible for a Top 3 placement at that venue. Age 11 students are strongly discouraged from performing en pointe."]},{"Key":"registration","Title":"How to Register","Items":["Register online on {{Website}}. Watch the step-by-step registration videos first: {{RegistrationTutorials}}.","To enter as a dancer representing a school, set up an Individual account and get your school's 36-digit studio code before you start registering. Only the school representative can give this code, from the school's dashboard. YAGP cannot give the code or link accounts.","A school or studio may register all its participants. All ensembles must be registered through a school or studio account.","A dancer in an Individual account must use the school's 36-digit ID before the first registration. If the code is not used before the first registration, the account cannot be linked to the school later.","If a school registers the students and the students pay on their own: the school representative registers all students. The students then log in to the school account with the login details sent by the registration system to their e-mail, check the information, and make a partial or full payment.","A completed waiver must be on file before the payment section. Follow the waiver tutorial on the YAGP tutorials page.","YAGP is not responsible for the information entered by participants or their representatives. Check that everything entered is correct.","After registration and full payment, log in to the account dashboard and check all details. Use the tutorial on how to confirm your registration.","A dancer who registers through several accounts (for example an Individual account for solos and a School account for ensembles) must tell YAGP about the multiple registration fees before making the second payment. YAGP is not responsible for fees paid twice and gives no refund.","Registration closes when a venue reaches its capacity. A dancer may register for the Wait List of that location instead. No payment is taken for the wait list, and YAGP tries to place everyone.","All updates, including TBD entries, must be received by the update deadline: {{UpdateDeadline}}. Penalties apply. The registration system closes for editing after the 30-day deadline.","A dancer who wants to perform a classical variation not on the list should check with the judges: it is the judge's decision whether it suits the dancer's age and skill.","Teacher badges: independent dancers and schools with up to 3 students get 1 badge, schools with 4 or more students get 2. Complete the Teacher Badge Google Form for your event (sent to the registration e-mail) before the deadline. Badges are given only to the teachers named in the form, not to the name in the Teacher field of the registration, and e-mail requests are not accepted.","A teacher badge is a free pass to watch the competition in the theater and to attend Open Stage with the dancer. It is picked up at the Welcome Table by showing a valid ID. A badge is given only if the teacher's name appears on the school website.","Teachers must not be backstage or in the dressing rooms without need; the theater may ask everyone to leave if it is crowded. Parents do not get teacher badges and may not go backstage or to the dressing rooms. A Pre-Competitive dancer without a teacher should visit the Welcome Table for help."]},{"Key":"fees","Title":"Fees","Items":["Fees depend on when all fees are paid in full. A registration/administrative fee applies: {{AdminFee}}. It guarantees your place and includes free master classes at each semi-final.","In order to reserve space at a location, YAGP must receive the registration fee deposit of $125 per dancer, per location, at the first registration.","If there is no payment within 30 days of the first registration, the registration is no longer valid and you must register again.","If a venue is wait-listed, YAGP can ask for full payment. The fee schedule does not apply to wait list registration.","Early bird (pay in full before the deadlines): {{EarlyBirdDiscount}}. Solo {{EarlyBirdSolo}}; contemporary-long solo {{EarlyBirdContemporaryLong}}; classical pas de deux {{EarlyBirdClassicalPDD}}; contemporary pas de deux {{EarlyBirdContemporaryPDD}}; duet/trio {{EarlyBirdDuetTrio}}; small ensemble {{EarlyBirdSmallEnsemble}}; large ensemble {{EarlyBirdLargeEnsemble}}.","Regular fees: solo {{RegularSolo}}; contemporary-long solo {{RegularContemporaryLong}}; classical pas de deux {{RegularClassicalPDD}}; contemporary pas de deux {{RegularContemporaryPDD}}; duet/trio {{RegularDuetTrio}}; small ensemble {{RegularSmallEnsemble}}; large ensemble {{RegularLargeEnsemble}}.","Late registration fees: solo {{LateSolo}}; contemporary-long solo {{LateContemporaryLong}}; classical pas de deux {{LateClassicalPDD}}; contemporary pas de deux {{LateContemporaryPDD}}; duet/trio {{LateDuetTrio}}; small ensemble {{LateSmallEnsemble}}; large ensemble {{LateLargeEnsemble}}.","A contemporary solo over 2:00 (up to 2:30) costs extra: {{ContemporaryLongSurcharge}}.","Finals fees are flat fees that include the registration processing fee, all master classes, special events, and free admission to all Finals activities including the Final Round and Gala. Semi-final fees cannot be moved to the Finals payment and partial payment is not accepted. Soloist (Junior and Senior) {{FinalsSoloFee}}; soloist (Pre-Competitive) {{FinalsPreCompFee}}; classical pas de deux {{FinalsClassicalPDDFee}}; contemporary pas de deux {{FinalsContemporaryPDDFee}}; ensemble {{FinalsEnsembleFee}}.","Additional fees for each extra ensemble entry at the Finals: {{FinalsExtraFees}}.","Watch the independent payment and studio payment video tutorials on the YAGP tutorials page."]},{"Key":"dates","Title":"Dates and Deadlines","Items":["Semi-final venues and dates: {{SemiFinalVenues}}.","Early bird: Fall 2025 venues, register and pay in full before {{EarlyBirdFallDeadline}} (by 31 July 2025). Winter/Spring 2026 venues, before {{EarlyBirdWinterSpringDeadline}} (by 31 August 2025).","Regular fees: Fall 2025 venues, register and pay in full after 31 July 2025. Winter/Spring 2026 venues, after 31 August 2025.","Late registration: {{LateRegistrationDates}}.","Payment: {{PaymentDeadline}}.","Updates and TBD entries: {{UpdateDeadline}}. Penalties apply.","Music: {{MusicDeadline}}. Penalties apply.","Props approval: {{PropsApprovalDeadline}}. To approve props at the Finals, add them in the Notes section of the registration.","Credit from an injury or illness must be used before {{CreditUseDate}}."]},{"Key":"levels","Title":"Semi-Finals and Finals","Items":["To take part in the Finals, a dancer must be selected at one of the YAGP semi-final events (competitions, auditions or workshops).","A solo entry needs a total score of 96 or higher in the Classical Ballet category. At the judges' choice, solo dancers with less than 96 on a classical variation may also be invited to the Finals.","A score of 96 or higher in the Contemporary/Open category does not guarantee selection for the Finals.","Finals: Junior and Senior dancers must register with 1 classical variation and 1 contemporary solo, once invited.","To qualify for the Finals, each Junior and Senior dancer must perform at least one classical variation from the list. Pre-Competitive dancers may qualify in Classical Ballet, Contemporary Dance or both.","It is strongly suggested that dancers register for the Finals with the same variation they were selected with, but they may choose any variation from the Classical Repertoire List.","1st, 2nd or 3rd place at a regional semi-final does not guarantee selection for the Finals, because these places are given relative to the other performances in each category.","Pre-Competitive dancers qualify for the Finals with a total score of 96 or higher for any solo. Only pieces that score 96 or higher can enter the Finals, and a dancer may choose at most two pieces for the Finals: 1 classical and 1 contemporary.","Ensemble entries are invited to the Finals at the judges' choice or with a total score of 96.","At the Finals, schools may not perform ensembles longer than the time limit, including extended time or double ensemble pieces. A longer ensemble is not allowed to perform and no refund is given. Two ensembles from the same school are not scheduled next to each other."]},{"Key":"judging","Title":"Judging and Scoring","Items":["Scoring has two elements, artistic and technical, evaluated on a 100-point system.","Each judge's score is the average of the technical and artistic marks. The total score is the average of the scores of all judges, who come from different backgrounds. There are usually three to five judges at each regional semi-final.","Judges may write personal comments on the score sheet to guide the dancer's training.","All scoring results are done electronically and sent to the registration e-mail address shortly after the event.","Awards ceremonies are held live, or online (date and time announced by e-mail for each location) if travel or health rules restrict a live event.","Categories may be announced separately or together, at the judges' choice. If fewer than 6 male soloists compete in the same age category, male and female soloists are combined in that category.","Small and large ensembles may be combined or separated at the judges' choice. If fewer than 6 classical and contemporary pas de deux compete, they are combined in the ensemble category.","Ensembles may be separated by age category (Junior and Senior) or by entry type (Classical or Contemporary) at the judges' choice. Junior ensembles: average age up to 13. Senior ensembles: average age 14 and up. Classical: chosen from the classical repertoire (en pointe or not). Contemporary: no music restrictions (en pointe or not).","Dancers who, by consensus of the jury, were better than all other dancers in their age division in both Classical Ballet and Contemporary/Open Dance may receive the Hope, Youth Grand Prix or Grand Prix Award. To be considered, a dancer must perform both a classical variation and a contemporary/open solo."]},{"Key":"prizes","Title":"Prizes and Awards","Items":["Top places at each semi-final are announced, including 1st, 2nd and 3rd place and the Top 12. The rules print no prize amounts.","The Grand Prix Award is for the best overall performance in the Senior age division.","The Youth Grand Prix Award is for the best overall performance in the Junior age division.","The Hope Award is for the best overall performance in the Pre-Competitive age division.","The jury may decide not to give all the announced awards."]},{"Key":"points","Title":"Placings and Winning Places","Items":["No points are printed for placings.","A dancer may not receive a winning placement at more than one location. The only exception is a dancer who places higher than at the earlier venue.","Example: a dancer who has placed in the Top 12 at one semi-final cannot place in the Top 12 at another location unless they place 1st, 2nd or 3rd."]},{"Key":"teams","Title":"Ensembles and Pas de Deux","Items":["For pas de deux entries where the male dancer is 14 or younger, it is strongly encouraged that the piece uses par terre partnering only, with no lifting above shoulder level.","Entries by size: duet/trio (2-3 members), ensemble of 4 members, ensemble of 5 or more members, classical pas de deux and contemporary pas de deux."]},{"Key":"conduct","Title":"Conduct and Penalties","Items":["YAGP can deduct points from any entry or dancer that does not follow the rules and regulations.","Music that is longer than the time limit can lead to point deduction or disqualification. Dancers may not buy extra time.","Music by Kerry Muzzey is strictly forbidden at all YAGP events because of music copyright rules.","Music sent less than 2 weeks before the first day of the competition: {{LateMusicPenalty}}.","Music sent or updated during the competition weekend: {{OnsiteMusicPenalty}}.","Updating TBD entries after the 30-day deadline: {{TbdPenalty}}.","Dancers may not perform the Pharaoh's Daughter Aspecia variation (Act 2) without written permission from the Lacotte Foundation. Permission is given only to dancers aged 15 and up and is requested through {{RegionalOffice}}. Any other Pierre Lacotte variation (including Marco Spada) is strictly forbidden. Dancers without permission are not allowed on stage and no refund is given.","Choreography by Frederick Ashton, the Etudes (H. Lander) Ballerina's Variation and the Gamzatti Temple Variation (N. Makarova) may only be performed with express written permission from the rights holders or the managing trusts or foundations, for YAGP Regionals, Finals or co-produced Galas."]},{"Key":"complaints","Title":"Refunds, Credits and Financial Aid","Items":["YAGP has a no-refund policy. Fees are non-refundable and non-transferable.","The registration/administrative fee is non-creditable, non-refundable and non-transferable for any reason: {{AdminFee}}.","Credit is given only to an injured participant, less the $125 registration fee per dancer, per location, and must be used before {{CreditUseDate}}. It covers only the entry fee(s) and only for a physical injury.","A request for credit needs an official letter from a specialist doctor (a family doctor's letter is not accepted) on the office letterhead, with an ink signature and the doctor's stamp, sent to {{FinanceOffice}} no later than 2 weeks before the first competition date. If YAGP is told later than that, only 50% of the entry fees are given as credit.","A dancer who is not injured but cannot attend because of illness can move the entry fee(s), less the $125 registration fee, to another convenient location if space is available. A doctor's note is needed, the same letter rules apply, and the credit must be used before {{CreditUseDate}}.","Financial aid: a dancer in financial hardship sends an official letter request to {{FinanceOffice}}. Financial aid is for one venue per season."]},{"Key":"other","Title":"Other Topics in the Rules","Items":["Music: use the YAGP Classical Music Library on the website for classical variation music, as it is made for live-streaming copyright rules. Tracks can be adjusted for tempo changes or cut.","A dancer may use their own music file for a classical variation that is not in the library. The video may be muted online for copyright issues, but the track is not muted on stage in the theater.","Upload music in the registration account: on the dashboard click Upload Music (the same steps update or replace music). Files must be .mp3 or .m4a. Check that the file appears after upload.","Name solo music files 'Last Name First Name - AGE - Name of the Dance'. Name pas de deux and ensemble files 'Name of the Dance - PDD or Ens or Duet or Trio - School Name - length of the music'.","Music sent or updated during the competition weekend is accepted only on a USB drive with the entry number.","Time limits: classical variation 2:30 (the Paquita Wedding variation can be up to 2:42); contemporary/open solo recommended 2:00, up to 2:30 for an extra fee; classical pas de deux 6:00 (Adagio, or Adagio and Coda only); contemporary pas de deux 3:30; duet/trio 2:45; ensemble of 4 3:30; ensemble of 5 or more 5:00.","When registering online, choose Option 1 (short, recommended limit 2:00, standard fee) or Option 2 (long, 2:30, extra fee) for a contemporary solo.","Pre-Competitive dancers performing en demi-pointe may perform any variation from the Junior repertoire list in addition to the Pre-Competitive list.","Pre-Competitive teachers may make small changes to the original classical choreography to suit the dancer's technical level."]}],"Documents":[{"Title":"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations (PDF)","Url":"https://yagp.org/misc/Downloads/2026/YAGP_Rules_and_Regulations.pdf"}]}`),t=[{ParticipantType:"Individual",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 2, 15, 17, 18",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Classical variation: 2:30 maximum.","Contemporary/Open solo: recommended 2:00, up to 2:30 for an extra fee."],Rules:["Soloists choose Classical Ballet, Contemporary/Open Dance, or both.","Classical Ballet: choose the variation from the Classical Repertoire List for the age group.","Each Junior and Senior dancer must perform at least one classical variation to qualify for the Finals. Pre-Competitive dancers may qualify in classical or contemporary, or both.","A dancer may not receive a winning placement at more than one location unless they place higher than before."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["A total score of 96 or higher in the Classical Ballet category is needed for selection to the Finals (judges may invite others)."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Classical variation: 2:30 maximum.
- Contemporary/Open solo: recommended 2:00, up to 2:30 for an extra fee.

## Rules
- Soloists choose Classical Ballet, Contemporary/Open Dance, or both.
- Classical Ballet: choose the variation from the Classical Repertoire List for the age group.
- Each Junior and Senior dancer must perform at least one classical variation to qualify for the Finals. Pre-Competitive dancers may qualify in classical or contemporary, or both.
- A dancer may not receive a winning placement at more than one location unless they place higher than before.

## Points
- A total score of 96 or higher in the Classical Ballet category is needed for selection to the Finals (judges may invite others).`},{ParticipantType:"Team",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 2, 3, 10, 17, 18",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:null,Rules:["The average age of the dancers in an ensemble or pas de deux must be between 9 and 20.","Professional dancers may not be a partner in an ensemble or pas de deux.","All ensembles must be registered through a school or studio account.","Ensembles may be Junior (average age up to 13) or Senior (average age 14 and up), and Classical or Contemporary, at the judges' choice.","For Finals, ensembles may not be longer than the time limit. Two ensembles from the same school are not scheduled next to each other.","Ensembles are invited to the Finals at the judges' choice or with a total score of 96."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Rules
- The average age of the dancers in an ensemble or pas de deux must be between 9 and 20.
- Professional dancers may not be a partner in an ensemble or pas de deux.
- All ensembles must be registered through a school or studio account.
- Ensembles may be Junior (average age up to 13) or Senior (average age 14 and up), and Classical or Contemporary, at the judges' choice.
- For Finals, ensembles may not be longer than the time limit. Two ensembles from the same school are not scheduled next to each other.
- Ensembles are invited to the Finals at the judges' choice or with a total score of 96.`}],i=JSON.parse(`[{"AgeGroup":"Pre-Competitive","Source":"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 2, 3, 11, 15, 18","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Age 9-11 (born between 2 January 2014 and 1 January 2017). Age is counted on {{SeasonAgeDate}}.","Dancers use the Pre-Competitive Classical Repertoire List. Their teachers may make slight changes to the classical choreography to suit the dancer's level.","Dancers performing en demi-pointe may also perform any variation from the Junior list.","Students aged 10 and under may not perform en pointe. If they do, they are not eligible for a Top 3 placement at that venue. Age 11 students are strongly discouraged from en pointe.","Pre-Competitive dancers may qualify for the Finals in Classical Ballet or Contemporary Dance, or both, with a total score of 96 or higher.","At most two pieces may go to the Finals: 1 classical and 1 contemporary.","The Hope Award is for the best overall performance in this division."],"Allowed":["Classical Repertoire List, Pre-Competitive age category: Coppelia (A. St. Leon) 1st Act Variation; Don Quixote (M. Petipa) Cupid Variation; Fairy Doll (S. Legat); Flower Festival at Genzano (A. Bournonville) Pas de Deux Variations; Giselle (J. Perrot, J. Coralli) Peasant Pas de Deux Variations; Graduation Ball (D. Lichine) Pas De Deux Variations; Harlequinade (M. Petipa) Pas De Deux Variations; La Bayadere (M. Petipa) Three Shade Variations; La Fille Mal Gardee (B. Nijinska, D. Romanoff) Pas de Deux Variations; Le Corsaire (M. Petipa) Odalisque Variations; Paquita (M. Petipa) All Variations (except Principal Variations); Raymonda (M. Petipa) All Variations (except Principal Variations); Swan Lake (M. Petipa, L. Ivanov) Pas de Trois Variations; The Flames of Paris (V. Vainonen) Pas de Deux Variations; The Sleeping Beauty (M. Petipa) Variations of Fairies, Blue Bird Pas de Deux Variations."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Age 9-11 (born between 2 January 2014 and 1 January 2017). Age is counted on {{SeasonAgeDate}}.\\n- Dancers use the Pre-Competitive Classical Repertoire List. Their teachers may make slight changes to the classical choreography to suit the dancer's level.\\n- Dancers performing en demi-pointe may also perform any variation from the Junior list.\\n- Students aged 10 and under may not perform en pointe. If they do, they are not eligible for a Top 3 placement at that venue. Age 11 students are strongly discouraged from en pointe.\\n- Pre-Competitive dancers may qualify for the Finals in Classical Ballet or Contemporary Dance, or both, with a total score of 96 or higher.\\n- At most two pieces may go to the Finals: 1 classical and 1 contemporary.\\n- The Hope Award is for the best overall performance in this division.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Classical Repertoire List, Pre-Competitive age category: Coppelia (A. St. Leon) 1st Act Variation; Don Quixote (M. Petipa) Cupid Variation; Fairy Doll (S. Legat); Flower Festival at Genzano (A. Bournonville) Pas de Deux Variations; Giselle (J. Perrot, J. Coralli) Peasant Pas de Deux Variations; Graduation Ball (D. Lichine) Pas De Deux Variations; Harlequinade (M. Petipa) Pas De Deux Variations; La Bayadere (M. Petipa) Three Shade Variations; La Fille Mal Gardee (B. Nijinska, D. Romanoff) Pas de Deux Variations; Le Corsaire (M. Petipa) Odalisque Variations; Paquita (M. Petipa) All Variations (except Principal Variations); Raymonda (M. Petipa) All Variations (except Principal Variations); Swan Lake (M. Petipa, L. Ivanov) Pas de Trois Variations; The Flames of Paris (V. Vainonen) Pas de Deux Variations; The Sleeping Beauty (M. Petipa) Variations of Fairies, Blue Bird Pas de Deux Variations."},{"AgeGroup":"Junior","Source":"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 2, 3, 15, 17, 18","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Age 12-14 (born between 2 January 2011 and 1 January 2014). Age is counted on {{SeasonAgeDate}}.","A Junior dancer must perform at least one classical variation to qualify for the Finals and must register with 1 classical variation and 1 contemporary solo once invited.","The Youth Grand Prix Award is for the best overall performance in this division. A dancer must perform both a classical variation and a contemporary/open solo to be considered.","Pharaoh's Daughter (P. Lacotte) is strictly prohibited for the Junior category."],"Allowed":["Classical Repertoire List, Junior age category: Coppelia (A. St. Leon) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Diana & Acteon (A. Vaganova) Pas de Deux and Variations - only for 14 year olds; Don Quixote (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Fairy Doll (S. Legat); Flower Festival at Genzano (A. Bournonville) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Giselle (J. Perrot, J. Coralli) Variation of Giselle, Act I Peasant Pas de Deux and Variations, Pas de Deux Variations from Act II; Graduation Ball (D. Lichine) Pas De Deux Variations; Harlequinade (M. Petipa) Pas De Deux and Variations; La Bayadere (M. Petipa) Three Shade Variations, Act III; Gamzatti Variation, Pas de Deux and Variations, Bronze Idol, Nikia Variation (Nikia Variation is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40; Gamzatti Temple Variation (choreography N. Makarova) is NOT accepted without permission from N. Makarova); La Esmeralda (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; La Fille Mal Gardee (B. Nijinska, D. Romanoff) Pas de Deux and all Variations; La Ventana (A. Bournonville) All Variations; La Sylphide (A. Bournonville) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Laurencia (V. Chabukiani); Le Corsaire (M. Petipa) Pas d'Esclave and Variations, Odalisque Variations, Jardin Anime, Act III Pas de Deux and Variations; Les Sylphides/Chopiniana (M. Fokine) Male and Female Mazurkas, Waltz # 7 and Waltz # 11, Prelude; Napoli (A. Bournonville) Pas de Six and all Variations; Paquita (M. Petipa) All Variations (Paquita Etoile is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40 minutes); Raymonda (M. Petipa) All Variations; Satanella (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and Variations; Swan Lake (M. Petipa, L. Ivanov) Pas de Trois and Variations; The Awakening of Flora (M. Petipa) Variations; The Flames of Paris (V. Vainonen) Pas de Deux and Variations; The Nutcracker Suite (V. Vainonen) Pas de Deux and Variations; The Sleeping Beauty (M. Petipa) Variations of Fairies, Aurora Variations from Act I and Act II (under 2:40), BlueBird Pas de Deux and Variations, Wedding Pas de Deux and Variations (Aurora Variation from Act I is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40); The Cavalry Halt (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; The Talisman (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; William Tell variation (A. Bournonville)."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Age 12-14 (born between 2 January 2011 and 1 January 2014). Age is counted on {{SeasonAgeDate}}.\\n- A Junior dancer must perform at least one classical variation to qualify for the Finals and must register with 1 classical variation and 1 contemporary solo once invited.\\n- The Youth Grand Prix Award is for the best overall performance in this division. A dancer must perform both a classical variation and a contemporary/open solo to be considered.\\n- Pharaoh's Daughter (P. Lacotte) is strictly prohibited for the Junior category.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Classical Repertoire List, Junior age category: Coppelia (A. St. Leon) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Diana & Acteon (A. Vaganova) Pas de Deux and Variations - only for 14 year olds; Don Quixote (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Fairy Doll (S. Legat); Flower Festival at Genzano (A. Bournonville) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Giselle (J. Perrot, J. Coralli) Variation of Giselle, Act I Peasant Pas de Deux and Variations, Pas de Deux Variations from Act II; Graduation Ball (D. Lichine) Pas De Deux Variations; Harlequinade (M. Petipa) Pas De Deux and Variations; La Bayadere (M. Petipa) Three Shade Variations, Act III; Gamzatti Variation, Pas de Deux and Variations, Bronze Idol, Nikia Variation (Nikia Variation is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40; Gamzatti Temple Variation (choreography N. Makarova) is NOT accepted without permission from N. Makarova); La Esmeralda (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; La Fille Mal Gardee (B. Nijinska, D. Romanoff) Pas de Deux and all Variations; La Ventana (A. Bournonville) All Variations; La Sylphide (A. Bournonville) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Laurencia (V. Chabukiani); Le Corsaire (M. Petipa) Pas d'Esclave and Variations, Odalisque Variations, Jardin Anime, Act III Pas de Deux and Variations; Les Sylphides/Chopiniana (M. Fokine) Male and Female Mazurkas, Waltz # 7 and Waltz # 11, Prelude; Napoli (A. Bournonville) Pas de Six and all Variations; Paquita (M. Petipa) All Variations (Paquita Etoile is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40 minutes); Raymonda (M. Petipa) All Variations; Satanella (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and Variations; Swan Lake (M. Petipa, L. Ivanov) Pas de Trois and Variations; The Awakening of Flora (M. Petipa) Variations; The Flames of Paris (V. Vainonen) Pas de Deux and Variations; The Nutcracker Suite (V. Vainonen) Pas de Deux and Variations; The Sleeping Beauty (M. Petipa) Variations of Fairies, Aurora Variations from Act I and Act II (under 2:40), BlueBird Pas de Deux and Variations, Wedding Pas de Deux and Variations (Aurora Variation from Act I is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40); The Cavalry Halt (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; The Talisman (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; William Tell variation (A. Bournonville)."},{"AgeGroup":"Senior","Source":"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 2, 3, 15, 17, 18","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["Age 15-20 (born between 2 January 2006 and 1 January 2011). Age is counted on {{SeasonAgeDate}}.","A Senior dancer must perform at least one classical variation to qualify for the Finals and must register with 1 classical variation and 1 contemporary solo once invited.","The Grand Prix Award is for the best overall performance in this division. A dancer must perform both a classical variation and a contemporary/open solo to be considered.","Pharaoh's Daughter (P. Lacotte): only one variation is allowed, only with permission, and only for Senior women: the 2nd Act Aspecia Variation."],"Allowed":["Classical Repertoire List, Senior age category: Coppelia (A. St. Leon) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Diana & Acteon (A. Vaganova) Pas de Deux and Variations; Don Quixote (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Fairy Doll (S. Legat); Flower Festival at Genzano (A. Bournonville) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Giselle (J. Perrot, J. Coralli) Variation of Giselle, Act I Peasant Pas de Deux and Variations, Pas de Deux Variations from Act II; Graduation Ball (D. Lichine) Pas De Deux Variations; Grand Pas Classique (V. Gsovsky) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Harlequinade (M. Petipa) Pas De Deux and Variations; La Bayadere (M. Petipa) Three Shade Variations, Act III; Gamzatti Variation, Pas de Deux and Variations, Bronze Idol, Nikia Variation (Nikia Variation is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40; Gamzatti Temple Variation (choreography N. Makarova) is NOT accepted without permission from N. Makarova); La Esmeralda (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; La Fille Mal Gardee (B. Nijinska, D. Romanoff) Pas de Deux and all Variations; La Ventana (A. Bournonville) All Variations; La Sylphide (A. Bournonville) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Laurencia (V. Chabukiani); Le Corsaire (M. Petipa) Pas d'Esclave and Variations, Odalisque Variations, Jardin Anime, Act III Pas de Deux and Variations; Les Sylphides/Chopiniana (M. Fokine) Male and Female Mazurkas, Waltz # 7 and Waltz # 11, Prelude; Napoli (A. Bournonville) Pas de Six and all Variations; Pharaoh's Daughter (P. Lacotte) Only one variation allowed and only with permission (only open to Senior Women): 2nd Act Aspecia Variation. Request the rights holder's e-mail from YAGP; Paquita (M. Petipa) All Variations (Paquita Etoile is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40); Raymonda (M. Petipa) All Variations; Satanella (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and Variations; Swan Lake (M. Petipa, L. Ivanov) Pas de Trois and Variations, Odette's Variation, Act II Black Swan Pas de Deux and Variations; The Awakening of Flora (M. Petipa) Variations; The Flames of Paris (V. Vainonen) Pas de Deux and Variations; The Nutcracker Suite (V. Vainonen) Pas de Deux and Variations; The Sleeping Beauty (M. Petipa) Variations of Fairies, Aurora Variations from Act I and Act II (under 2:30), BlueBird Pas de Deux and Variations, Wedding Pas de Deux and Variations (Aurora Variation from Act I is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40); The Cavalry Halt (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; The Talisman (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Walpurgis Nacht (L. Lavrovsky) Pas de Deux and Variations; William Tell variation (A. Bournonville)."],"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- Age 15-20 (born between 2 January 2006 and 1 January 2011). Age is counted on {{SeasonAgeDate}}.\\n- A Senior dancer must perform at least one classical variation to qualify for the Finals and must register with 1 classical variation and 1 contemporary solo once invited.\\n- The Grand Prix Award is for the best overall performance in this division. A dancer must perform both a classical variation and a contemporary/open solo to be considered.\\n- Pharaoh's Daughter (P. Lacotte): only one variation is allowed, only with permission, and only for Senior women: the 2nd Act Aspecia Variation.\\n\\n## Allowed\\n- Classical Repertoire List, Senior age category: Coppelia (A. St. Leon) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Diana & Acteon (A. Vaganova) Pas de Deux and Variations; Don Quixote (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Fairy Doll (S. Legat); Flower Festival at Genzano (A. Bournonville) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Giselle (J. Perrot, J. Coralli) Variation of Giselle, Act I Peasant Pas de Deux and Variations, Pas de Deux Variations from Act II; Graduation Ball (D. Lichine) Pas De Deux Variations; Grand Pas Classique (V. Gsovsky) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Harlequinade (M. Petipa) Pas De Deux and Variations; La Bayadere (M. Petipa) Three Shade Variations, Act III; Gamzatti Variation, Pas de Deux and Variations, Bronze Idol, Nikia Variation (Nikia Variation is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40; Gamzatti Temple Variation (choreography N. Makarova) is NOT accepted without permission from N. Makarova); La Esmeralda (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; La Fille Mal Gardee (B. Nijinska, D. Romanoff) Pas de Deux and all Variations; La Ventana (A. Bournonville) All Variations; La Sylphide (A. Bournonville) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Laurencia (V. Chabukiani); Le Corsaire (M. Petipa) Pas d'Esclave and Variations, Odalisque Variations, Jardin Anime, Act III Pas de Deux and Variations; Les Sylphides/Chopiniana (M. Fokine) Male and Female Mazurkas, Waltz # 7 and Waltz # 11, Prelude; Napoli (A. Bournonville) Pas de Six and all Variations; Pharaoh's Daughter (P. Lacotte) Only one variation allowed and only with permission (only open to Senior Women): 2nd Act Aspecia Variation. Request the rights holder's e-mail from YAGP; Paquita (M. Petipa) All Variations (Paquita Etoile is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40); Raymonda (M. Petipa) All Variations; Satanella (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and Variations; Swan Lake (M. Petipa, L. Ivanov) Pas de Trois and Variations, Odette's Variation, Act II Black Swan Pas de Deux and Variations; The Awakening of Flora (M. Petipa) Variations; The Flames of Paris (V. Vainonen) Pas de Deux and Variations; The Nutcracker Suite (V. Vainonen) Pas de Deux and Variations; The Sleeping Beauty (M. Petipa) Variations of Fairies, Aurora Variations from Act I and Act II (under 2:30), BlueBird Pas de Deux and Variations, Wedding Pas de Deux and Variations (Aurora Variation from Act I is not accepted for competition, unless under 2:40); The Cavalry Halt (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; The Talisman (M. Petipa) Pas de Deux and all Variations; Walpurgis Nacht (L. Lavrovsky) Pas de Deux and Variations; William Tell variation (A. Bournonville)."},{"AgeGroup":"Ensemble","Source":"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 2, 3, 10, 17","Sections":{"About":null,"TimeAndFormat":null,"Rules":["The average age of the dancers must be between 9 and 20. Dancers younger or older may take part if the average is in range.","Professional dancers cannot be partners.","Pas de deux with a male dancer aged 14 or younger: par terre partnering only is strongly encouraged, with no lifting above shoulder level.","Ensembles may be separated into Junior (average age up to 13) and Senior (average age 14 and up) at the judges' choice."],"Allowed":null,"NotAllowed":null,"Judging":null,"Points":null,"Notes":null},"Markdown":"## Rules\\n- The average age of the dancers must be between 9 and 20. Dancers younger or older may take part if the average is in range.\\n- Professional dancers cannot be partners.\\n- Pas de deux with a male dancer aged 14 or younger: par terre partnering only is strongly encouraged, with no lifting above shoulder level.\\n- Ensembles may be separated into Junior (average age up to 13) and Senior (average age 14 and up) at the judges' choice."}]`),o=[{Title:"Classical Variation",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 2, 9, 10, 15, 18",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Maximum 2:30. The Paquita Wedding variation can be up to 2:42.","Dancers may not buy extra time. Longer music can lead to point deduction or disqualification."],Rules:["Choose the variation from the Classical Repertoire List for the age group. The dancer is responsible for getting approval for any choreography that needs it.","A variation that is not on the list is at the judge's choice for age and skill. At the Finals the jury may ask the dancer to change to a variation from the list.","Use the YAGP Classical Music Library for the music if possible, or your own file."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["A total score of 96 or higher is needed for selection to the Finals. Judges may also invite dancers with a lower score."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Maximum 2:30. The Paquita Wedding variation can be up to 2:42.
- Dancers may not buy extra time. Longer music can lead to point deduction or disqualification.

## Rules
- Choose the variation from the Classical Repertoire List for the age group. The dancer is responsible for getting approval for any choreography that needs it.
- A variation that is not on the list is at the judge's choice for age and skill. At the Finals the jury may ask the dancer to change to a variation from the list.
- Use the YAGP Classical Music Library for the music if possible, or your own file.

## Points
- A total score of 96 or higher is needed for selection to the Finals. Judges may also invite dancers with a lower score.`},{Title:"Contemporary/Open Solo",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 2, 5, 10, 18",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Recommended maximum 2:00. Up to 2:30 is allowed for an extra {{ContemporaryLongSurcharge}}.","Choose Option 1 (short) or Option 2 (long) when registering."],Rules:["Any non-classical ballet solo. Music may include appropriate lyrics."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:["A score of 96 or higher does not guarantee selection for the Finals."],Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Recommended maximum 2:00. Up to 2:30 is allowed for an extra {{ContemporaryLongSurcharge}}.
- Choose Option 1 (short) or Option 2 (long) when registering.

## Rules
- Any non-classical ballet solo. Music may include appropriate lyrics.

## Points
- A score of 96 or higher does not guarantee selection for the Finals.`},{Title:"Classical Pas de Deux",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 2, 10",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Maximum 6:00 (Adagio, or Adagio and Coda only)."],Rules:["Choose a pas de deux from the Classical Repertoire List. Only the Adagio and Coda may be performed."],Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Maximum 6:00 (Adagio, or Adagio and Coda only).

## Rules
- Choose a pas de deux from the Classical Repertoire List. Only the Adagio and Coda may be performed.`},{Title:"Contemporary Pas de Deux",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 10, 17",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["Maximum 3:30."],Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- Maximum 3:30.`},{Title:"Duet/Trio",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 5, 10",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["2-3 members. Maximum 2:45."],Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- 2-3 members. Maximum 2:45.`},{Title:"Ensemble (4 Dancers)",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 5, 10",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["4 members. Maximum 3:30."],Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- 4 members. Maximum 3:30.`},{Title:"Ensemble (5+ Dancers)",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 5, 10",Sections:{About:null,TimeAndFormat:["5 or more members. Maximum 5:00."],Rules:null,Allowed:null,NotAllowed:null,Judging:null,Points:null,Notes:null},Markdown:`## Time and format
- 5 or more members. Maximum 5:00.`}],r=[],s=[{Key:"Website",Kind:"link",Label:"YAGP website",Value:"http://www.yagp.org",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 2"},{Key:"RegistrationTutorials",Kind:"link",Label:"Registration video tutorials",Value:"https://yagp.org/registration-tutorials/",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 4"},{Key:"FinanceOffice",Kind:"contact",Label:"Financial office (financial aid, injury and illness letters)",Value:{Name:"YAGP Financial office",Role:"Financial aid requests and doctor's letters",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"finance@yagp.org"},Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 7"},{Key:"RegionalOffice",Kind:"contact",Label:"Regional office (permission for restricted choreography)",Value:{Name:"YAGP Regional office",Role:"Written permission for the Pharaoh's Daughter (Aspecia) variation",Phone:"",WhatsApp:"",Email:"regional@yagp.org"},Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 15"},{Key:"SeasonAgeDate",Kind:"text",Label:"Date on which ages are counted for the whole 2026 season",Value:"1 January 2026",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 2"},{Key:"SemiFinalVenues",Kind:"text",Label:"Semi-final venues and dates",Value:"Not printed in the rules. Fall 2025 venues and Winter/Spring 2026 venues are listed on the YAGP website",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 5 and 6"},{Key:"AdminFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Registration/administrative fee (per dancer, per location)",Value:"$125, non-refundable, non-transferable and non-creditable; due at initial registration",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"EarlyBirdSolo",Kind:"fee",Label:"Early bird: classical or contemporary-short solo",Value:"$125 per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"EarlyBirdContemporaryLong",Kind:"fee",Label:"Early bird: contemporary-long solo (up to 2:30)",Value:"$145 per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"EarlyBirdClassicalPDD",Kind:"fee",Label:"Early bird: classical pas de deux",Value:"$125 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"EarlyBirdContemporaryPDD",Kind:"fee",Label:"Early bird: contemporary pas de deux",Value:"$85 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"EarlyBirdDuetTrio",Kind:"fee",Label:"Early bird: duet/trio",Value:"$80 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"EarlyBirdSmallEnsemble",Kind:"fee",Label:"Early bird: small ensemble (4 dancers)",Value:"$65 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"EarlyBirdLargeEnsemble",Kind:"fee",Label:"Early bird: large ensemble (5+ members)",Value:"$55 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"RegularSolo",Kind:"fee",Label:"Regular: classical or contemporary-short solo",Value:"$135 per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"RegularContemporaryLong",Kind:"fee",Label:"Regular: contemporary-long solo (up to 2:30)",Value:"$155 per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"RegularClassicalPDD",Kind:"fee",Label:"Regular: classical pas de deux",Value:"$130 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"RegularContemporaryPDD",Kind:"fee",Label:"Regular: contemporary pas de deux",Value:"$90 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"RegularDuetTrio",Kind:"fee",Label:"Regular: duet/trio",Value:"$85 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"RegularSmallEnsemble",Kind:"fee",Label:"Regular: small ensemble (4 dancers)",Value:"$70 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"RegularLargeEnsemble",Kind:"fee",Label:"Regular: large ensemble (5+ members)",Value:"$60 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"LateSolo",Kind:"fee",Label:"Late: classical or contemporary-short solo",Value:"$145 per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"LateContemporaryLong",Kind:"fee",Label:"Late: contemporary-long solo (up to 2:30)",Value:"$165 per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"LateClassicalPDD",Kind:"fee",Label:"Late: classical pas de deux",Value:"$135 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"LateContemporaryPDD",Kind:"fee",Label:"Late: contemporary pas de deux",Value:"$95 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"LateDuetTrio",Kind:"fee",Label:"Late: duet/trio",Value:"$90 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"LateSmallEnsemble",Kind:"fee",Label:"Late: small ensemble (4 dancers)",Value:"$75 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"LateLargeEnsemble",Kind:"fee",Label:"Late: large ensemble (5+ members)",Value:"$65 per dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"EarlyBirdDiscount",Kind:"fee",Label:"Early bird discount",Value:"$10 off per solo dancer, per entry; $5 off per ensemble dancer, per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"FinalsSoloFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Finals fee: soloist, Junior and Senior",Value:"$380 per dancer",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5 Finals Fees"},{Key:"FinalsPreCompFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Finals fee: soloist, Pre-Competitive",Value:"$335 per dancer",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5 Finals Fees"},{Key:"FinalsClassicalPDDFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Finals fee: classical pas de deux",Value:"$350 per dancer",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5 Finals Fees"},{Key:"FinalsContemporaryPDDFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Finals fee: contemporary pas de deux",Value:"$340 per dancer",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5 Finals Fees"},{Key:"FinalsEnsembleFee",Kind:"fee",Label:"Finals fee: ensemble",Value:"$230 per dancer",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5 Finals Fees"},{Key:"FinalsExtraFees",Kind:"fee",Label:"Finals: each additional ensemble entry, per dancer",Value:"Pas de deux $115; duet/trio $65; small ensemble (4 dancers) $60; ensemble (5 or more dancers) $50",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5 Finals Fees"},{Key:"ContemporaryLongSurcharge",Kind:"fee",Label:"Extra fee for a contemporary solo over 2:00 (up to 2:30)",Value:"$20 per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 5 and 10"},{Key:"LateMusicPenalty",Kind:"fee",Label:"Music submitted less than 2 weeks before the competition",Value:"$20 penalty per entry",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 7 and 9"},{Key:"OnsiteMusicPenalty",Kind:"fee",Label:"Music submitted or updated during the competition weekend",Value:"$30 penalty per entry, paid on site at the Registration table (USB drive with the entry number only)",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 7 and 9"},{Key:"TbdPenalty",Kind:"fee",Label:"Updating TBD entries after the 30-day deadline",Value:"$20 penalty per entry, added to the invoice (also $20 per entry for TBD updated during the competition weekend)",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 7"},{Key:"EarlyBirdFallDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Early bird for Fall 2025 venues: register and pay in full before",Value:"2025-08-01",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5 (by 31 July 2025)"},{Key:"EarlyBirdWinterSpringDeadline",Kind:"date",Label:"Early bird for Winter/Spring 2026 venues: register and pay in full before",Value:"2025-09-01",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5 (by 31 August 2025)"},{Key:"LateRegistrationDates",Kind:"text",Label:"Late registration starts (register and pay in full after)",Value:"Fall venues: after 31 August 2025. January venues: after 30 September 2025. February venues: after 31 October 2025. March venues: after 30 November 2025",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 5"},{Key:"CreditUseDate",Kind:"date",Label:"Credit for injury or illness must be used before",Value:"2026-03-01",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 7"},{Key:"UpdateDeadline",Kind:"text",Label:"Last day for entry updates (including TBD entries)",Value:"30 days before the competition weekend, or as stated in e-mails from YAGP",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 6"},{Key:"MusicDeadline",Kind:"text",Label:"Music submission deadline",Value:"2 weeks before the first day of the competition, or as stated in e-mails from YAGP. Do not submit updated music less than 1 week before the venue",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 6"},{Key:"PaymentDeadline",Kind:"text",Label:"Payment after registering",Value:"At least $125 per dancer or full payment at initial registration. Without full payment within 30 days of initial registration the registration is removed by the system and you must register again",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 5 and 6"},{Key:"PropsApprovalDeadline",Kind:"text",Label:"Props must be approved no later than",Value:"3 weeks before the first competition day",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations section 16"},{Key:"Notice",Kind:"news",Label:"Notice printed at the top of the rules",Value:[{Date:"",Title:"New contemporary solo time limit",Text:"The new recommended time limit for all Contemporary/Open Solos this season is a maximum of 2:00. Solos up to 2:30 are allowed for an extra $20 per entry.",Url:""}],Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations sections 5 and 10"}],l=[{Claim:"Rules, fees, deadlines, penalties, repertoire lists and awards are taken from the organiser's own 2026 rules document.",SourceType:"Primary - the event's own rules document",Source:"YAGP 2026 Rules and Regulations",Url:"https://yagp.org/misc/Downloads/2026/YAGP_Rules_and_Regulations.pdf"}],u={TemplateKey:e,Year:2026,Note:a,Page:n,ParticipantTypes:t,AgeGroups:i,Competitions:o,CompetitionAgeGroups:r,Variables:s,Evidence:l};export{i as AgeGroups,r as CompetitionAgeGroups,o as Competitions,l as Evidence,a as Note,n as Page,t as ParticipantTypes,e as TemplateKey,s as Variables,d as Year,u as default};
